  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Design and Monitoring Framework</narrative>
   </title>
   <document-link format="APPLICATION/PDF" url="https://www.adb.org/sites/default/files/project-documents/56069/56069-001-rrp-en.pdf">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reports and Recommendations of the President</narrative>
    </title>
    <category code="A08"></category>
    <language code="EN"></language>
    <document-date iso-date="2025-06-30+08:00"></document-date>
   </document-link>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1. To improve access and clarity of state-funded benefits offered to the population for PHC, specialized outpatient and diagnostic benefits, the government: (i) enhanced the benefits package of PHC services, ensuring that included services are patient-centered, gender-sensitive, and responsive to the population&#x2019;s health needs, especially to the needs of the poor, women, and vulnerable groups; (i) defined beneficiary groups that are eligible for free PHC and state-subsidized specialized care and diagnostic services, giving more benefits and greater financial protection to the poor, women, and vulnerable groups; and (ii) through MOH defined and approved the phased introduction of the enhanced PHC benefit package following the PHC roadmap developed with WHO support.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.1. To improve and ensure a continuum of health service provision for the patient across levels of care, the government through MOH established the gatekeeping function for PHC with clinical care pathways for four most-prevalent noncommunicable disease conditions to regulate referrals from primary care to specialized outpatient, diagnostic, and hospital services, and to significantly reduce patient self-referrals.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.2. To enhance strategic purchasing capacity of the single purchaser, the government through MOH introduced quality-based selection criteria for selective contracting of: (i) PHC service providers; and (ii) specialty outpatient care, and diagnostic services.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">3.1. To eliminate existing governance deficiencies in digital health data production and use, the government through MOH defined the institutional roles and responsibilities for digital health stewardship and coordination, to eliminate the current proliferation of different and conflicting digital standards, duplication and conflicting roles, including for cyber security, patient data, and record safety</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">4.1. To address existing gaps in PHC governance, the government through MOH defined the institutional roles and responsibilities for PHC stewardship and coordination, which will eliminate the current deficiencies and help advance the PHC reform agenda</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">4.2. To address quality of care by promoting evidence-based clinical decision making and prevent the use of outdated clinical approaches, the government through MOH established the National Council for the development, approval, and regulation of clinical practices guidelines, protocols, and clinical pathways revision</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">4.3. To address poor and sub-standard quality or unsafe medical services, and ensure sustained prevention of errors and adverse effects, the government through MOH approved the Patient Safety Program</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">4.4. To ensure effective public financial management and control system in MOH and its subordinated agency, the government introduced and signed an &#x201C;Agreement on Provision of Services within the Budget Program&#x201D; (in line with MOF methodology and guidance) between MOH and Georgian Medical Holding related to the budget programs encompassing PHC services and coordinating referrals to specialty care and diagnostic services for rural residents.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">4.5. To ensure readiness of public health response to extreme weather and heatwaves, the government through MOH approved the Heat-Health Action Plan.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Loan 4444: 0% of contracts awarded and 49% disbursed as of 30 Apr 2025</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
